   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Alembic camera import (S2-S3)\n\n**What it does**\nReads an animated camera from an **.abc** (Nuke, Maya, Houdini, Blender) into the shot camera every atlas-vfx node uses, then checks it against the camera our Nuke builder exported.\n\n**Try**\n- Point *source_path* at any .abc. If it holds several cameras, type one in *abc_camera* (e.g. `AVFX_Camera`).\n- *offset_first_frame*: **to 1**, **to 1001** or **to plate start** renumbers the camera before *crop_to_plate*. Use it only when the camera starts where the plate starts.\n- To see the renumber: **to 1** with *crop_to_plate* off gives frames 1-598.\n- Maya scenes in cm: *m_per_unit* 0.01.\n\n**Expect** (this file)\n168 frames 1130-1297, focal 16.47 mm, Solve Compare 0.00 % / 0.00 deg against the reference.\n\nCameras are saved to `atlas-vfx-work\\DSCF3000\\camera`."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
